==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|body politique||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{af|en|body|politic|pos2=postpositive adjective}}, {{cal|en|la|[[corpus]] [[polīticum]]|nocap=1}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|bodies politic}}

# {{lb|en|metaphorical}} The collective body of a [[nation]] or [[state]] as politically organized.
#* {{RQ:Hobbes Leviathan|page=115|chapter=Of Systems Subject Political and Private|passage=In '''Bodies Politique''' the power of the Repreſentative is alwaies Limited: And that which preſcribeth the Limits thereof, is the Power Soveraign.}}
#* {{RQ:Arendt Totalitarianism|page=14|passage=In contrast to all other groups, the Jews were defined and their position determined by the '''body politic'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kathryn Harrison|title=The Body Politic|work=The New York Times|date=2014-02-07|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/09/books/review/the-queens-bed-by-anna-whitelock.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=While most historians of the period dissect the '''body politic''', Whitelock doesn’t waste time in the halls of Parliament. Instead, she hastens straight to the boudoir of the queen who chose celibacy as a means of wielding power.}}
# {{lb|en|metaphorical}} The collective body of a nation or state as exercising political functions.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[corporation]].

